-- NeverQuest path data: where you can walk, per zone, in cells about 33 yards square.
--   [uiMapID] = { w, h (cells), yw, yh (the zone map's size in yards), cells, east, southeast, south, southwest }
-- All five strings run left to right, top to bottom, run-length coded: a count (none = 1), then a letter.
--   cells: the ground where you'd stand in the cell. a: open; b, c: a little rough; d: deep water, you
--     swim; e, f: a hillside; g: a scramble, or a climb the terrain doesn't hold (a lift, a ramp);
--     h: lava, tar or slime; i: too steep to walk; "." no ground at all.
--   east .. southwest: what the walk from this cell's spot to that neighbour's costs, measured on the
--     fine map (8-yard squares), in cells of open ground: letter n (a = 0) is 2^((n - 4) / 4), so
--     e = 1 (flat, straight across), g = 1.41 (flat, corner to corner), and z = 38 (over a cliff);
--     "." = no way. The other four directions are the neighbours' own (west is the west cell's east).
--   Since 1.28.4: before, a cell had one cost and any two neighbours were joined, which let a route
--   cross a ridge that happened to run between two mostly open cells.
-- Worked out from the game's own terrain (ground heights and liquids, read the way the OpenMap addon's
-- tools read them: github.com/Mapster-Addon/OpenMap, MIT) and checked against QuestieDB's creature
-- positions. Only these derived grids are shipped, none of the game's art or data files.
